# BrowserOS runtime state
# The agent runtime moved from packages/browseros-agent to trios/agent-server.
# These three rules did not move with it, so the runtime's own state - a
# SQLite auth database, its WAL and its shm - stopped being ignored and was
# committed. That is why local-auth.sqlite-shm appeared as modified in every
# git status. The files are untracked in the same commit that fixes this.
trios/agent-server/.trinity/
trios/agent-server/apps/server/.trinity/
trios/agent-server/trios/

# Agent caches and build products
.agents/
.build/
.claude/worktrees/
# Sources/ is a grab-bag ignore alongside .build and .agents, but it also hides
# Sources/CSQLCipher - the module map Package.swift names as a systemLibrary
# target and build.sh cannot compile without. A clone of this repository failed
# on exactly those two files. Re-included by name; a manifest that declares a
# path the checkout can never contain is a dependency nobody can satisfy.
Sources/*
!Sources/CSQLCipher/
amp
OF

# Swift direct-compile artifacts from build.sh / swiftc.
#
# These were anchored to the repository root with a leading slash, for a tree
# where the build ran there. It runs in trios/ now, so `/*.o` stopped matching
# anything the compiler writes and the rule has been quietly inapplicable ever
# since. Found 2026-09-06 by the verdict audit: queen-1133 committed 24 object
# files as trios/*.o - one directory below the anchor - and `git check-ignore`
# agreed they were not ignored. Unanchored, so it holds wherever the build runs.
*.d
*.o
*.swiftdeps
